{"study_accession":"PRJNA923668","secondary_study_accession":"SRP417389","title":"Inherited CD19 deficiency impairs signaling in plasma cells","description":"Background: The human CD19 antigen is expressed throughout B cell ontogeny with the exception of neoplastic plasma cells and a subset of normal plasma cells. CD19 plays a role in propagating signals from the B cell receptor and other receptors such as CXCR4 in mature B cells. Studies of CD19-deficient patients have confirmed its function during the initial stages of B cell activation, however its role in the later stages of B cell differentiation is unclear. Objective: Using B cells from a newly identified CD19-deficient individual, we investigated the role of CD19 in the generation and function of plasma cells using an in vitro differentiation model. Overall design: RNA-seq","pubmed":"37246174","geo_series":"","n_samples":5,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN32730462","study_accession":"PRJNA923668","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"D13_CD19def","description":"D13_CD19def","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6934341","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-09-23","attributes":[["source_name","Peripheral blood"],["tissue","Peripheral blood"],["cell_type","Plasmacell"],["genotype","CD19def"],["time","D13"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR23075336","experiment_accession":"SRX19028360","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":56055177,"base_count":16816553100,"first_public":"2023-09-23","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM6934341: D13_CD19def Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN32730463","study_accession":"PRJNA923668","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"D10_CD19def","description":"D10_CD19def","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM6934340","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-09-